     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "In 2017 thieves came through the Paris catacombs (the old underground quarries) and drilled through the wall of a private apartment-building cellar in the 6th arrondissement, near the Luxembourg Gardens. Narration: 'Thieves tunnelled into a Paris wine cellar.' Headline 'A TUNNEL INTO / A PARIS WINE CELLAR'.",
     "urls": [
      "https://www.thelocal.fr/20170830/thieves-steal-300-bottles-of-wine-using-the-paris-catacombs",
      "https://www.foxnews.com/world/sour-grapes-robbers-empty-paris-cellar-of-vintage-wines",
      "https://www.decanter.com/wine-news/paris-catacombs-wine-theft-375377/",
      "https://www.thedrinksbusiness.com/2017/08/thieves-use-paris-catacombs-to-steal-wine/",
      "https://www.atlasobscura.com/articles/paris-theft-wine-catacombs-crime"
     ]
    },
    {
     "claim": "K_300",
     "type": "established",
     "claim_text": "About 300 bottles were taken (reports say 'about 300' / 'more than 300'; The Local's headline says 250), worth about EUR 250,000 (France Info via The Local; other outlets convert to $300,000-375,000). Narration (hook): 'And stole about 300 bottles.' Counter '300 BOTTLES', sub 'about EUR 250,000'.",
